                                        "sense_id": "c746ff5d-a10a-3814-be54-7161ace6ece3",
                                        "entry_id": "d595cd76-17f6-39d8-a258-9497bab029ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A transcontinental country in the Caucasus region of Europe and Asia, on the coast of the Black Sea, often considered to belong politically to Europe. Official name: Georgia. Capital: Tbilisi."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da7020d1-3b0c-42af-87ec-c43e7fef42a8",
                                                "sense_id": "c746ff5d-a10a-3814-be54-7161ace6ece3",
                                                "text": "Though this be held his laſt daies dꝛeadfull ſiege,\n Wherein he ſpareth neither man noꝛ childe,\n Yet are there Chꝛiſtians of Georgia here,\n Whoſe ſtate who euer pitied and relieu'd:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe2cab02-7c44-46d1-a161-68d2d22a0d8b",
                                                "sense_id": "c746ff5d-a10a-3814-be54-7161ace6ece3",
                                                "text": "The practice of raiſing ſlaves to the great offices of ſtate is ſtill more common among the Turks than among the Perſians. The miſerable countries of Georgia and Circaſſia ſupply rulers to the greateſt part of the eaſt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07d6c907-fa1c-4213-b5e7-71674c540609",
                                                "sense_id": "c746ff5d-a10a-3814-be54-7161ace6ece3",
                                                "text": "During our stay in Georgia Mr. Chmarsky's gremlin hardly operated at all, and that made us feel better toward him, and made him feel better toward us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Georgia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60e5432e-3cee-30a7-816d-6cf6b0bc8c9a",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c39660-bdf1-38d4-865e-eaa51cec0cfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state in the Southern United States. Capital: Atlanta. It is named for George II of Great Britain (1683–1760)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa983cc8-a22a-4230-bbc6-7e3261a91e49",
                                                "sense_id": "60e5432e-3cee-30a7-816d-6cf6b0bc8c9a",
                                                "text": "I said, Georgia, oh, Georgia\n No peace I find\n Just an old, sweet song\n Keeps Georgia on my mind"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2384ecc4-5c6a-4eff-8f00-d1cc15833dbf",
                                                "sense_id": "60e5432e-3cee-30a7-816d-6cf6b0bc8c9a",
                                                "text": "Collins and the Trump campaign on Wednesday celebrated the recount decision from the Georgia secretary of state as a victory for “integrity” and “transparency.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f90adf0b-6a05-4c59-a8e2-1c6eaf770c16",
                                                "sense_id": "60e5432e-3cee-30a7-816d-6cf6b0bc8c9a",
                                                "text": "The U.S. Chemical Safety and Hazard Investigation Board (CSB) has released an update on its investigation into the September 29 BioLab fire in Conyers, Georgia, that shrouded neighborhoods in chemical smoke for days and forced thousands of residents to shelter in place or evacuate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "319c4cc7-9d88-30c5-887d-2a0b71060909",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c39660-bdf1-38d4-865e-eaa51cec0cfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of University of Georgia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06b632f5-982e-4d4a-bc90-256981db4d29",
                                                "sense_id": "319c4cc7-9d88-30c5-887d-2a0b71060909",
                                                "text": "The legislation is named after Laken Riley, a 22-year old Georgia student who was killed last year while out for a run. An undocumented migrant from Venezuela was convicted and sentenced to life without parole in the case that reignited a national debate over immigration and crime."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
